{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-350040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350040" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350040" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3-9x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=3-9x,$ then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-9\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3-9x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3-9x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3-9x)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3-9x)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3-9x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3-9x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3-9x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3-9x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\frac{\\pi x}{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-346081" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346081" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=10x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{10}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(10x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡(10x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-2203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(10x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{4},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $2\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u))\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =4(-1+2) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-346368" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-346368" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({u}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡x}{3}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡x}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡x}{3}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡x}{3}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡x}{3}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡x}{3}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=7x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"] ["math" "7\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-10143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}2{csc}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /9$ | $\\pi /6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}2{csc}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}2{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi }$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=4{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=8x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}sec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\cdot 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350202" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350202" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-13533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=6{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=12x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /2$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\cdot 12x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350203" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350203" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350887" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350887" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(4)-\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5)=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nSo, differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\cdot 24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{6}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(6)-\\ln(5)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\cdot (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-73674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{4}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-350904" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-350904" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(4)-\\ln(3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb88a11e6d6e19bd0e727d6f9ac9249290bdeaa02f55c6fa40c0cc21ec049f34"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C"] ["math" "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "q-113998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/state.json" "file_sha256" "800b28e53c8c3e5c2182537848206a5a429c02fc71b3714b35ed28797e7227a7"} {"question" "e-464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 2 \\sin {\\left(\\dfrac x 3\\right)} \\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-464.json" "file_sha256" "4c83df02b3f79824d79fde8d3298628e8c18280dc3fb4b9920d705ee539f9731"} {"question" "e-464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\dfrac x 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac 1 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =3\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-464.json" "file_sha256" "4c83df02b3f79824d79fde8d3298628e8c18280dc3fb4b9920d705ee539f9731"} {"question" "e-465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 5 \\csc {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\cot {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-465.json" "file_sha256" "536c120fbc619c2b158ea970fc1f3e59544bd1c8a9da62bc288c2450d4431b79"} {"question" "e-465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 6\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =\\dfrac 1 6\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-465.json" "file_sha256" "536c120fbc619c2b158ea970fc1f3e59544bd1c8a9da62bc288c2450d4431b79"} {"question" "e-466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\sec^2\\left(x^3-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-466.json" "file_sha256" "5dbaf0265d1b13acc93a79d12579459a43bdeefc079da41aeda10848648bd77e"} {"question" "e-466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u = x^3 - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 3x^2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u = x^2\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-466.json" "file_sha256" "5dbaf0265d1b13acc93a79d12579459a43bdeefc079da41aeda10848648bd77e"} {"question" "e-467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/4} \\dfrac{\\tan x \\sec^2 x}{1+\\tan^2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-467.json" "file_sha256" "db02471074f16fa8b9e64424e3342ec9aa1da5c30b0a5fe6a5aef89adcb9cf93"} {"question" "e-467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(1+\\tan^2 x) = 2\\tan{x}\\sec^2 x.\n$$\n\nSo, let $u = 1+\\tan^2 x.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 2\\tan x\\sec^2 x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u = \\tan x\\sec^2 x\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-467.json" "file_sha256" "db02471074f16fa8b9e64424e3342ec9aa1da5c30b0a5fe6a5aef89adcb9cf93"}] "usage" {"q-10143" [] "e-467" [] "e-466" [] "e-465" [] "q-13647" [] "e-464" []} "basis" 1115 "retractions" [[17592186068972 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/8}5\\sin (4x)dx$?"] [17592186068929 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\sec (7x)\\tan (7x)dx$."] [17592186068491 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 2 \\sin {\\left(\\dfrac x 3\\right)} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068491 :question/worked-solution "If we let\n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac x 3\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac 1 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =3\\, \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int2\\sin (\\frac{x}{3})dx &= 2\\int\\sin u \\cdot 3du \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3\\int\\sin udu \\\\\n&=-6\\cos u + C \\\\\n&=-6\\cos (\\frac{x}{3}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068492 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 5 \\csc {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\cot {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068492 :question/worked-solution "If we let\n\n$$\nu=6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 6\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =\\dfrac 1 6\\, \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int5\\csc (6x + \\frac{π}{3})\\cot (6x + \\frac{π}{3})dx &= 5\\int\\csc (6x + \\frac{π}{3})\\cot (6x + \\frac{π}{3})dx \\\\\n&= 5\\int\\csc u\\cot u \\cdot \\frac{1}{6}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}\\int\\csc u\\cot udu \\\\\n&=-\\frac{5}{6}\\csc u + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{5}{6}\\csc (6x + \\frac{π}{3}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068493 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\sec^2\\left(x^3-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186068493 :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu = x^3 - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x} = 3x^2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u = x^2\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}\\sec^{2} (x^{3} - \\frac{π}{6})dx &= \\int\\sec^{2} (x^{3} - \\frac{π}{6}) \\cdot x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\sec^{2} (u) \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\int\\sec^{2} (u)du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\tan u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\tan (x^{3} - \\frac{π}{6}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068494 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/4} \\dfrac{\\tan x \\sec^2 x}{1+\\tan^2x}\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186068494 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(1+\\tan^2 x) = 2\\tan{x}\\sec^2 x\n$$\n\nSo, let\n\n$$\nu = 1+\\tan^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2\\tan x\\sec^2 x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u = \\tan x\\sec^2 x\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi/4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/4}\\frac{\\tan x\\sec^{2} x}{1 + \\tan^{2} x}dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\frac{1}{1 + \\tan^{2} x} \\cdot \\tan x\\sec^{2} xdx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\ln 2 - \\ln 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186065369 17592186065370 17592186065371 17592186065372 17592186065373 17592186065627 17592186065628 17592186065629 17592186065630 17592186065631] "immutable_fields" [[17592186065368 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065368 :answer-field/id] [17592186065368 :answer-field/key] [17592186065368 :answer-field/type] [17592186065626 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065626 :answer-field/id] [17592186065626 :answer-field/key] [17592186065626 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
